  … order ε²: −(1 − λ²/S)a²(1 − 2p)/(2S), at any lag (Hayward–Sella eq. 7) ok
  near p = 0 (c = 0): Kopp–Hermisson a(2λ − a)/(2S) + a²λ²/(2S²)           ok
  rare alleles, 2c term: Δc = −Σa⁴p/(2S) − c²/S to first order in each p   ok
  house of cards p ∝ g/a²: Σa⁴p = (Σga²/Σg)·Σa²p, i.e. α²c                 ok

(b) the neutral Poisson random field
  Wright–Fisher: E[p′q′] = (1 − 1/(2N)) pq                                 ok
  Σ_t (1 − 1/(2N))^t pq = 2N pq                                            ok
  diffusion: u = 2N pq solves (pq/(4N))u″ = −pq, u(0) = u(1) = 0           ok
  V_G = 2NLμ · 2α² · 2N p₀q₀ = (2N − 1) V_m                                ok
  implicit Euler step: V_G = (2N − 1/(2N)) V_m                             ok

(c) the response of the mean
  symmetric pair (±a at one p): Σ 2a E[Δp] = (Σ 2a²pq) λ/S                 ok
  directional part of Σ 2a E[Δp] is V_G λ/S, V_G = Σ 2a²pq                 ok

(d) the sweep variance
  logistic sweep: dp/dt = s pq                                             ok
  so d(p/s)/dt = pq: ∫ pq dt over the sweep = (1 − p₀)/s ≈ 1/s             ok
  ∫ 2a²pq dt = 2a²/s = 2a S/λ                                              ok
  Haldane 2s × 2aS/λ = 4a², whatever λ and S                               ok
  2NLμ · (N_e/N) · E[4a²; a > 0] = 2N_e V_m, with E[a²; a > 0] = α²/2      ok

(e) linked selection
  Var(Δp) = pq/(2n)·N/N_e with N/N_e = 1 + b²VΣ ⇔ pq(1/(2n) + c), c = b²VΣ/(2n) ok
  Barton per locus: (L − 1)·(b²V/L)/(2r²) = b²V·(1 − 1/L)/(2r²) (weights Σω = 1 − 1/L) ok
  ∂ln W̄/∂z̄ = λ/S = b (additive variance in relative fitness b²V)           ok

